      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2016. Published by Elsevier Masson SAS.",
        "AbstractText": "Teenagers need to interpret the world around them, sometimes in a completely different way to that in which, as children, they represented external reality. Some like drawing. They can use it to express their thoughts on death, sexuality or freedom. Their creative capacities are immense: they are creating art."
